## TypeScript Standards

### Type Safety
- **No `any` types** - use `unknown` if type is truly unknown
- Define interfaces for all props and API responses
- Use type guards for runtime type checking
- Leverage TypeScript's utility types: `Partial<T>`, `Pick<T>`, `Omit<T>`

### File Organization
```typescript
// types/api.ts - API response types
export interface Organization {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  description?: string;
  created_at: string;
}

// types/index.ts - Re-export commonly used types
export * from './api';
export * from './ui';
```

### Component Props
```typescript
// Always define props interface
interface CardProps {
  title: string;
  description?: string;
  children?: React.ReactNode;
  className?: string;
  onClick?: () => void;
}

// Use React.FC or explicit return type
export function Card({ title, description, children, className, onClick }: CardProps) {
  // ...
}
```

